<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">St. John River (Liberia)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The St. John River is a river of Liberia that rises in the Nimba highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a> and flows south-west to the Atlantic at Buchanan. At its mouth American colonisation societies from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pennsylvania">Pennsylvania</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> founded Port Cresson in the early 1830s, refounded as Bassa Cove, which later joined the Commonwealth of Liberia. The town there was renamed Buchanan after the governor Thomas Buchanan.</p></div>
